  "document": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Why small tools win | Example Blog</title>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Small, sharp tools outlast sprawling platforms. Here is why.\">\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Mira Okafor\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Why small tools win\">\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://blog.example.org/img/small-tools.jpg\">\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-05-14T09:30:00Z\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://blog.example.org/2024/05/why-small-tools-win\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Why small tools win\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Mira Okafor\"},\"datePublished\":\"2024-05-14T09:30:00Z\"}</script>\n<style>.hero{background:#fff}.nav a{color:#333}</style>\n</head>\n<body class=\"post single\">\n<header class=\"site-header\"><nav class=\"nav\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a> <a href=\"/archive\">Archive</a> <a href=\"/about\">About</a></nav></header>\n<main id=\"content\">\n<article class=\"post-content\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/BlogPosting\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\" itemprop=\"headline\">Why small tools win</h1>\n<p class=\"byline\">By <span class=\"author\">Mira Okafor</span> on <time datetime=\"2024-05-14\">May 14, 2024</time></p>\n<p>Every few years a platform promises to replace the ten tools on your desk with one. It rarely does. The tools that last are the ones that do one thing, expose it cleanly, and stay out of the way.</p>\n<h2 id=\"composition\">Composition beats configuration</h2>\n<p>A pipe between two programs is worth a thousand settings screens. When each piece has a narrow contract, you can swap one without ceremony. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_philosophy\">The Unix philosophy</a> is a good example, but the principle is older than Unix.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Make each program do one thing well.</p></blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"cost\">The hidden cost of breadth</h2>\n<p>Breadth has a carrying cost. Every feature is a promise to maintain, document and keep compatible. A <em>small</em> tool makes fewer promises and keeps more of them.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fewer moving parts</li>\n<li>Faster onboarding</li>\n<li>Cheaper to replace</li>\n</ul>\n<pre><code class=\"language-sh\">cat access.log | grep 500 | sort | uniq -c</code></pre>\n<p>None of this means big systems are wrong. It means each addition should <strong>earn</strong> its place.</p>\n</article>\n<aside class=\"sidebar widget-area\"><h3>Related</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/p/1\">Boring technology</a></li><li><a href=\"/p/2\">Cheap to change</a></li></ul></aside>\n<section class=\"comments\" id=\"comments\"><h3>3 comments</h3><ol class=\"comment-list\"><li class=\"comment\"><p>Great post!</p></li></ol></section>\n</main>\n<footer class=\"site-footer\"><p>© 2024 Example Blog. All rights reserved.</p><div class=\"newsletter-signup\">Subscribe</div></footer>\n<script>window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments)}</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
